WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.934 --> 00:00:02.100
-What a great audience!

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:03.968
-They love you.
-Thank you.

00:00:03.968 --> 00:00:06.334
-Come on.
-And I love you!

00:00:06.334 --> 00:00:07.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:07.934 --> 00:00:09.601
-It's all right!
We have to --

00:00:09.601 --> 00:00:11.000
[ Laughs ]

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:13.100
We have to talk to her! I know!
-Thank you.

00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:15.234
[ Cheers and applause
continues ]

00:00:15.234 --> 00:00:18.901
-Oh, my --

00:00:18.901 --> 00:00:20.300
I'm not gonna get time
to talk to you!

00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:21.467
-I know!

00:00:21.467 --> 00:00:23.200
I'm not gonna get any time
to talk to you!

00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:24.901
-Yeah.
Well, you better hush, then.

00:00:24.901 --> 00:00:25.968
[ Laughter ]
Okay.

00:00:25.968 --> 00:00:27.534
'Cause we gotta talk.
-We have to talk.

00:00:27.534 --> 00:00:29.667
All right.
So, we have a lot to discuss.

00:00:29.667 --> 00:00:31.200
First of all, congratulations.

00:00:31.200 --> 00:00:34.033
You were just inducted into
the Rock and Roll Hall of Fame.

00:00:34.033 --> 00:00:36.968
-Yes!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:36.968 --> 00:00:38.567
-I'm a rock star now.

00:00:38.567 --> 00:00:40.200
That's what they say.
-I mean --

00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:43.501
-That was such an honor.
You know?

00:00:43.501 --> 00:00:45.601
I'm making an album, too,
'cause I have to live up

00:00:45.601 --> 00:00:46.934
to all that hype.
-Yeah.

00:00:46.934 --> 00:00:48.667
[ Laughter ]

00:00:48.667 --> 00:00:50.033
-At first, you were nervous.

00:00:50.033 --> 00:00:51.267
You were like,
"I don't know, guys.

00:00:51.267 --> 00:00:53.534
What do you mean?
Rock 'n' roll? I don't know."

00:00:53.534 --> 00:00:55.167
-Well, honestly, I was sincere.

00:00:55.167 --> 00:00:57.501
I did not mean to start
any kind of controversy.

00:00:57.501 --> 00:00:59.067
But when they said
they wanted to put me

00:00:59.067 --> 00:01:00.634
in the
Rock and Roll Hall of Fame,

00:01:00.634 --> 00:01:02.467
I always thought that was
for people that spent

00:01:02.467 --> 00:01:04.734
their whole life working to be
in rock 'n' roll.

00:01:04.734 --> 00:01:07.334
And, you know, you don't see
Led Zeppelin

00:01:07.334 --> 00:01:08.601
in the Country Music
Hall of Fame.

00:01:08.601 --> 00:01:10.000
-Yeah.
[ Laughter ]

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:11.601
-I thought --
Although they could.

00:01:11.601 --> 00:01:13.534
But anyway, I found out
it was more than that.

00:01:13.534 --> 00:01:15.701
So when I realized what it was,
I said,

00:01:15.701 --> 00:01:17.834
"If they put me in anyway,
I would certainly

00:01:17.834 --> 00:01:19.634
accept it gracefully,"
which I did.

00:01:19.634 --> 00:01:21.167
Even wrote a song about it
to kind of

00:01:21.167 --> 00:01:23.300
tell the story about it.
-Yeah.

00:01:23.300 --> 00:01:24.567
The Zach Brown Band.
That was great.

00:01:24.567 --> 00:01:26.400
-I know.
But anyway, I'm very honored

00:01:26.400 --> 00:01:28.167
and very proud.
It did --

00:01:28.167 --> 00:01:30.400
I'm good about timing,
so I'd always thought

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:32.033
I might want to do a rock record

00:01:32.033 --> 00:01:34.067
'cause my husband
is a rock 'n' roll freak.

00:01:34.067 --> 00:01:36.234
-Yeah.
-So anyway, I thought,

00:01:36.234 --> 00:01:38.367
"Well, if I'm ever gonna do it,
now's the time."

00:01:38.367 --> 00:01:39.467
-So you're doing
a rock 'n' roll record?

00:01:39.467 --> 00:01:41.400
-I am. It's gonna come out
next fall.

00:01:41.400 --> 00:01:42.734
[ Cheers and applause ]
Yeah.

00:01:42.734 --> 00:01:44.634
And you know what
I'm calling it?

00:01:44.634 --> 00:01:47.100
-What's that?
-"Rock Star" is the name of it.

00:01:47.100 --> 00:01:49.934
-Yeah. Are you gonna have any
good duets or cameos on there?

00:01:49.934 --> 00:01:52.234
-Well, actually, I am going
to have a some cameo people.

00:01:52.234 --> 00:01:53.467
-People are watching
our show tonight.

00:01:53.467 --> 00:01:55.200
-I've written a few originals.
-Okay, good.

00:01:55.200 --> 00:01:57.567
And a couple originals.
-And we're gonna have a lot of

00:01:57.567 --> 00:01:59.734
great, iconic songs,
like "Purple Rain"

00:01:59.734 --> 00:02:02.367
and "Can't Get No Satisfaction."

00:02:02.367 --> 00:02:04.167
-Oh, my God!
That's what I'm talking about.

00:02:04.167 --> 00:02:06.968
-"Stairway to Heaven"
and "Free Bird."

00:02:06.968 --> 00:02:08.734
I'm even did "Free Bird."
-Oh, my gosh!

00:02:08.734 --> 00:02:10.167
I cannot wait for this.

00:02:10.167 --> 00:02:12.133
-But I'm gonna have
a few guest artists.

00:02:12.133 --> 00:02:13.434
-Okay, good.
-But anyway...

00:02:13.434 --> 00:02:14.701
-I'm looking forward to that.
Come back for that.

00:02:14.701 --> 00:02:15.968
Please do.
-All right.

00:02:15.968 --> 00:02:18.267
Well, I love singing with you.
I might have to --

00:02:18.267 --> 00:02:20.067
I might have to get you in the
Rock and Roll Hall of Fame.

00:02:20.067 --> 00:02:21.501
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:02:21.501 --> 00:02:22.667
-I'm probably gonna faint again.

00:02:22.667 --> 00:02:24.434
I want to talk about
our adventures.

00:02:24.434 --> 00:02:26.567
The other thing
I want to talk about, too, is,

00:02:26.567 --> 00:02:28.334
you and Miley are teaming up.

00:02:28.334 --> 00:02:30.167
You're co-hosting
New Year's Eve in Miami.

00:02:30.167 --> 00:02:31.300
[ Cheers and applause ]
-We are.

00:02:31.300 --> 00:02:34.300
In Miami, with Miley,
on New Year's Eve.

00:02:34.300 --> 00:02:36.133
Can you imagine that?
-I'm so excited.

00:02:36.133 --> 00:02:37.601
-We're gonna have great fun.
Yeah.

00:02:37.601 --> 00:02:39.167
-Yeah.
Do you like doing live?

00:02:39.167 --> 00:02:40.968
Do you get nervous or no?
-Oh, no.

00:02:40.968 --> 00:02:43.601
And Miley and I are so great --
She loves you, too, by the way.

00:02:43.601 --> 00:02:45.801
-Oh, no.
I say "too" because I love you.

00:02:45.801 --> 00:02:47.467
-[ Laughs ]
-Don't everybody?

00:02:47.467 --> 00:02:48.667
-You're my favorite.

00:02:48.667 --> 00:02:51.000
-Anyhow, we're gonna do
a great thing.

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:52.834
I'm sure we'll ad-lib
a whole lot of things,

00:02:52.834 --> 00:02:56.033
and we're gonna
do some songs together

00:02:56.033 --> 00:02:58.234
and a few rock things
with some of the artists

00:02:58.234 --> 00:02:59.467
she's gonna have there.

00:02:59.467 --> 00:03:01.467
Lord knows what could happen
with Miley and me.

00:03:01.467 --> 00:03:03.000
-Yeah, yeah, yeah.
Lord knows.

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:04.133
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:04.133 --> 00:03:07.467
-I love her.
Oh, you and me are the best!

00:03:07.467 --> 00:03:08.968
-How cute is this?
-I know.

00:03:08.968 --> 00:03:10.934
-I mean, that is the best thing
I've ever --

00:03:10.934 --> 00:03:12.601
I just thought it was so cute.

00:03:12.601 --> 00:03:14.701
I had the greatest time
doing this.

00:03:14.701 --> 00:03:17.200
-Yeah, this was great.
I think that's a great song.

00:03:17.200 --> 00:03:20.367
And I told him years ago,
I asked him to sing with me

00:03:20.367 --> 00:03:22.734
on another song, and he said,
"Oh, I don't really

00:03:22.734 --> 00:03:24.501
think of myself
as a serious singer.

00:03:24.501 --> 00:03:25.601
I just like to have fun."

00:03:25.601 --> 00:03:27.734
I said,
"I think you're a great singer."

00:03:27.734 --> 00:03:30.634
So, anyway, we recorded,
last year, Mariah's song,

00:03:30.634 --> 00:03:31.934
or year before last.

00:03:31.934 --> 00:03:34.834
But then this year,
he sent me this song and said,

00:03:34.834 --> 00:03:36.300
"Would you do a duet with me?"

00:03:36.300 --> 00:03:38.067
And I said, "Well, absolutely."

00:03:38.067 --> 00:03:39.701
And so we did it.
-We did it.

00:03:39.701 --> 00:03:42.167
-We did it in the show, too.
-So I thought, I go,

00:03:42.167 --> 00:03:43.801
"Let's do a song
that's almost a little bit

00:03:43.801 --> 00:03:45.767
too early for Christmas."
-Yeah, I love that.

00:03:45.767 --> 00:03:47.801
-And we'll release it
in October.

00:03:47.801 --> 00:03:49.100
And so --
[ Laughter ]

00:03:49.100 --> 00:03:51.868
So, we put it out
right before Halloween,

00:03:51.868 --> 00:03:56.033
and it went to number one
on the Apple iTunes charts.

00:03:56.033 --> 00:03:57.300
-Yes!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:03:57.300 --> 00:04:00.601
♪♪

00:04:00.601 --> 00:04:02.634
-We have a number-one hit song!
-I know!

00:04:02.634 --> 00:04:04.033
I'm so excited.

00:04:04.033 --> 00:04:06.367
-Releasing a holiday song
in October works. Who knew?

00:04:06.367 --> 00:04:07.801
-But that's a great song,
by the way.

00:04:07.801 --> 00:04:09.701
-No, you made it into a song.

00:04:09.701 --> 00:04:11.234
I gave you nothing,
and you're like,

00:04:11.234 --> 00:04:13.300
"Oh, watch me do this."
-Oh, sure. Yeah.

00:04:13.300 --> 00:04:15.000
I did my part.
-Can we talk about the special?

00:04:15.000 --> 00:04:16.901
Because I had the greatest time
hanging out.

00:04:16.901 --> 00:04:20.100
I got to hang out with Dolly
for a full...two days?

00:04:20.100 --> 00:04:22.634
-Yeah, full two days.
-It was great.

00:04:22.634 --> 00:04:25.334
"Dolly Parton's
Mountain Magic Christmas."

00:04:25.334 --> 00:04:27.868
It airs tomorrow night on NBC,
8:00.

00:04:27.868 --> 00:04:29.801
Everyone, set your DVRs.
Tape this thing.

00:04:29.801 --> 00:04:31.367
Watch this thing.
Have a party.

00:04:31.367 --> 00:04:32.801
It's awesome.
I'm in it.

00:04:32.801 --> 00:04:33.934
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Yeah.

00:04:33.934 --> 00:04:35.467
You did great, too.
And we loved having you.

00:04:35.467 --> 00:04:37.133
-We did well, right?

00:04:37.133 --> 00:04:38.901
Willie Nelson's in it.
You and Willie.

00:04:38.901 --> 00:04:40.934
-Miley.
-Miley Cyrus is in it.

00:04:40.934 --> 00:04:43.601
Jimmie Allen's in it.
-Jimmie Allen.

00:04:43.601 --> 00:04:45.534
-It's a big giant special.
-Jimmy Fallon.

00:04:45.534 --> 00:04:46.767
-Jimmie Allen, Jimmy Fallon.
It rhymes.

00:04:46.767 --> 00:04:48.100
[ Laughter ]

00:04:48.100 --> 00:04:51.033
-Yeah, and Zach Williams,
who I had a Grammy Award song,

00:04:51.033 --> 00:04:53.267
"There was Jesus," one of my
favorite songs on the album.

00:04:53.267 --> 00:04:57.000
-Your sisters, too.
-And my sisters, and my nieces.

00:04:57.000 --> 00:04:58.501
My sisters Cassie and Rachel
are there.

00:04:58.501 --> 00:05:00.200
I couldn't round
the rest of them up.

00:05:00.200 --> 00:05:02.934
I got a bunch of them.
But anyway...

00:05:02.934 --> 00:05:05.200
We did a whole family thing,
and it was just wonderful.

00:05:05.200 --> 00:05:08.367
-So, I flew to Tennessee
to meet you.

00:05:08.367 --> 00:05:10.434
-Whoo!
-There you go.

00:05:10.434 --> 00:05:11.734
We allow four people
from Tennessee

00:05:11.734 --> 00:05:13.400
every night to come in
to the show.

00:05:13.400 --> 00:05:14.601
There they are,
sitting right up there.

00:05:14.601 --> 00:05:16.033
-Oh, that's sweet.
-Yeah, it's nice of us.

00:05:16.033 --> 00:05:17.467
-Hey, there!

00:05:17.467 --> 00:05:20.234
-So, I was so excited
because we were filming

00:05:20.234 --> 00:05:22.000
in Dollywood.
-Yeah.

00:05:22.000 --> 00:05:25.100
-At Dollywood!
Which I was blown away!

00:05:25.100 --> 00:05:26.467
-I know.
Didn't it make a great --

00:05:26.467 --> 00:05:28.701
We got everything.
There's, like, a movie set.

00:05:28.701 --> 00:05:31.267
Anything that you could need.
It's a paradise.

00:05:31.267 --> 00:05:33.767
I'm very proud of it.
-So I land in Tennessee,

00:05:33.767 --> 00:05:35.968
and I wanted to just get there
so I can drive around.

00:05:35.968 --> 00:05:38.033
I wanted to go to Sevierville,
where you grew up

00:05:38.033 --> 00:05:40.634
and see all your --
You know, just get a little

00:05:40.634 --> 00:05:42.501
Dolly love and spread it around.

00:05:42.501 --> 00:05:44.501
I got to pose next
to your statue, by the way.

00:05:44.501 --> 00:05:47.167
-Oh, yeah, I heard you did that.
-Yeah, I saw your statue

00:05:47.167 --> 00:05:49.501
right before you, yeah.
I saw you.

00:05:49.501 --> 00:05:51.901
-In my bare feet.
-In your bare feet.

00:05:51.901 --> 00:05:53.300
-That's the only time
you'll ever catch me

00:05:53.300 --> 00:05:54.567
out of my high heels.
-That's right.

00:05:54.567 --> 00:05:56.000
-I've got bare feet.
-That's your bare feet.

00:05:56.000 --> 00:05:58.133
That's the only time.
So, here's what happened.

00:05:58.133 --> 00:06:00.501
I didn't have a driver.
I didn't set up a car.

00:06:00.501 --> 00:06:02.501
So, I just called an Uber,
right?

00:06:02.501 --> 00:06:04.033
So I get in the --
I just call an Uber.

00:06:04.033 --> 00:06:05.634
-You call it a Goober
if you were up there.

00:06:05.634 --> 00:06:08.701
-[ Laughs ] Yeah!
I got a Goober.

00:06:08.701 --> 00:06:11.334
I called --
I went on the Goober app.

00:06:11.334 --> 00:06:13.968
So, I go on Uber,
and this guy shows up.

00:06:13.968 --> 00:06:16.467
His name is Chad, so shout-out
to Chad if he's watching.

00:06:16.467 --> 00:06:20.834
And I get in the car,
and he goes, "Oh, wow."

00:06:20.834 --> 00:06:23.033
He goes, "I just got --
before I start the car,

00:06:23.033 --> 00:06:24.400
I'm just freaking out right now.

00:06:24.400 --> 00:06:26.868
I didn't know it was you,
and I've never met a celebrity.

00:06:26.868 --> 00:06:29.634
This is just bizarre for me,
so just give me a second."

00:06:29.634 --> 00:06:32.767
I go, "Yeah, no problem, Chad.
Take as much time as you want."

00:06:32.767 --> 00:06:34.467
[ Laughter ]
So, he starts the car.

00:06:34.467 --> 00:06:36.100
He was really nice.
So, we're driving through,

00:06:36.100 --> 00:06:37.501
he's talking about you,
and we're talking about

00:06:37.501 --> 00:06:39.300
how great you are
and we love you.

00:06:39.300 --> 00:06:40.634
And I'm there,
and I just landed,

00:06:40.634 --> 00:06:41.667
you must have heard
that I landed,

00:06:41.667 --> 00:06:42.901
so you called me.

00:06:42.901 --> 00:06:45.067
-Oh, yeah,
to see if you was here.

00:06:45.067 --> 00:06:46.801
-You call me, and you go,
"Jimmy, how you doing?

00:06:46.801 --> 00:06:49.601
You landed in Tennessee?"
And all I see is Chad going...

00:06:49.601 --> 00:06:54.000
[ Laughter ]

00:06:54.000 --> 00:06:56.133
And I go, "Chad!
Stay on the road, buddy!"

00:06:56.133 --> 00:06:57.367
He's like -- He's freaking out.

00:06:57.367 --> 00:06:59.901
He goes, "Was that
Dolly Parton on the phone?"

00:06:59.901 --> 00:07:02.868
He's like, "This is
the greatest drive of my life!"

00:07:02.868 --> 00:07:05.334
And it was so fun.
-And you had barbecue.

00:07:05.334 --> 00:07:07.734
-Yeah, I went and had barbecue,
and then we rehearsed.

00:07:07.734 --> 00:07:10.501
We danced together.
-Everybody loved you.

00:07:10.501 --> 00:07:13.434
And when you left --
I mean, you just brought --

00:07:13.434 --> 00:07:15.300
It was just like somebody
flipped the lights off

00:07:15.300 --> 00:07:16.467
in Booger Town.
[ Laughter ]

00:07:16.467 --> 00:07:18.167
-Really?
-Like, everybody --

00:07:18.167 --> 00:07:21.467
There's a place up there called
Booger Town, right in that area.

00:07:21.467 --> 00:07:24.801
So, but, anyway, everybody said,
"He is the nicest guy."

00:07:24.801 --> 00:07:27.000
And I said, "You know,
you don't know the half of it."

00:07:27.000 --> 00:07:29.300
But everybody said,
"Well, did you tell him

00:07:29.300 --> 00:07:31.868
our famous story
about our bear?"

00:07:31.868 --> 00:07:35.167
And I said, "No, I never
got a chance to tell that."

00:07:35.167 --> 00:07:36.334
Do you have time for it
on the show?

00:07:36.334 --> 00:07:39.300
-Yeah, please.
-Well, this is a true story.

00:07:39.300 --> 00:07:42.334
Up in Pigeon Forge
is where we were.

00:07:42.334 --> 00:07:45.534
And I know you asked me
why they call it Pigeon Forge,

00:07:45.534 --> 00:07:48.601
and I told it's because
that's where pigeons forge.

00:07:48.601 --> 00:07:50.100
But anyway...
-Thank you for that.

00:07:50.100 --> 00:07:52.300
-There's the Pigeon River,
and I guess the pigeons --

00:07:52.300 --> 00:07:54.400
-Foot in mouth.
There you go, yeah, thank you.

00:07:54.400 --> 00:07:56.033
[ Laughter ]
-But seriously,

00:07:56.033 --> 00:07:57.968
in Pigeon Forge, many years ago,

00:07:57.968 --> 00:08:01.067
back when I was a kid,
they had a bear in a cage.

00:08:01.067 --> 00:08:03.501
You know, we're famous
for the bears in the Smokies.

00:08:03.501 --> 00:08:05.667
And they had a bear
in a big cage up there.

00:08:05.667 --> 00:08:08.334
And people would stop
at this market,

00:08:08.334 --> 00:08:11.901
and they would buy Cokes for
this bear that was in the cage.

00:08:11.901 --> 00:08:14.300
And tourists would take pictures

00:08:14.300 --> 00:08:16.100
'cause Gatlinburg,
that whole area.

00:08:16.100 --> 00:08:20.334
For years, you know,
they would put Cokes and peanuts

00:08:20.334 --> 00:08:23.100
in the Coca-Cola cans
or whatever the --

00:08:23.100 --> 00:08:25.033
Bottled Cokes were then.

00:08:25.033 --> 00:08:28.033
So, anyway, this bear was just
getting bigger and bigger.

00:08:28.033 --> 00:08:30.534
But they were doing that,
and they were just selling

00:08:30.534 --> 00:08:32.634
all kinds of stuff
at this market.

00:08:32.634 --> 00:08:34.767
And this poor bear
was just drinking them all.

00:08:34.767 --> 00:08:38.667
And one day, some redneck put --
[ Laughter ]

00:08:38.667 --> 00:08:39.934
No, seriously.

00:08:39.934 --> 00:08:43.667
They put gasoline in a Coke can.
[ Audience "Awws" ]

00:08:43.667 --> 00:08:45.634
Can you believe
how bad people are?

00:08:45.634 --> 00:08:47.501
And the poor thing
just went crazy.

00:08:47.501 --> 00:08:51.367
And it broke out of the pen,

00:08:51.367 --> 00:08:53.033
and it started towards
Sevierville

00:08:53.033 --> 00:08:55.300
because Pigeon Forge is about
eight miles from Sevierville.

00:08:55.300 --> 00:08:57.601
And it just ran
all the way down there,

00:08:57.601 --> 00:08:59.501
you know, and it was
just going down there.

00:08:59.501 --> 00:09:02.133
And all of a sudden,
it just fell over.

00:09:02.133 --> 00:09:03.667
-Oh.
-I know.

00:09:03.667 --> 00:09:04.767
-Dead?

00:09:04.767 --> 00:09:06.334
-No.
It was out of gas.

00:09:06.334 --> 00:09:08.667
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:09:08.667 --> 00:09:12.934
♪♪

00:09:12.934 --> 00:09:14.834
-I love you!

00:09:14.834 --> 00:09:16.601
[ Applause continues ]

00:09:16.601 --> 00:09:20.434
I love you!
I love you so much!

00:09:20.434 --> 00:09:23.501
You are the greatest!

00:09:23.501 --> 00:09:26.934
Ah, she got me!
Hook, line, and sinker!

00:09:26.934 --> 00:09:30.501
-Yeah.
-It is so fun to hang out.

00:09:30.501 --> 00:09:32.567
"Dolly Parton's
Mountain Magic Christmas."

00:09:32.567 --> 00:09:35.267
The special is about
bringing that magic back.

00:09:35.267 --> 00:09:36.501
What are we missing?

00:09:36.501 --> 00:09:39.467
The love, the coziness
of the Smoky Mountains

00:09:39.467 --> 00:09:40.767
and all the fun.

00:09:40.767 --> 00:09:43.067
It is so fun.
There's music, there's dancing.

00:09:43.067 --> 00:09:45.133
-Yeah, a lot of comedy.
A lot of kids stuff.

00:09:45.133 --> 00:09:47.467
So, something for everybody,
so be sure to watch it.

00:09:47.467 --> 00:09:49.868
Lot of meaningful things.
-I loved --

00:09:49.868 --> 00:09:52.367
I'll never forget hanging out
with you as long as I live.

00:09:52.367 --> 00:09:54.667
I had so much fun with you.
And we danced from --

00:09:54.667 --> 00:09:56.334
I'm not kidding,
and I wish it was different,

00:09:56.334 --> 00:09:58.501
but we danced
from 10:00 to 3:00.

00:09:58.501 --> 00:10:00.067
Almost 9:00 to 5:00.
-It wore me out.

00:10:00.067 --> 00:10:01.601
[ Laughter ]
-10:00 a.m. --

00:10:01.601 --> 00:10:04.334
10:00 a.m. to 3:00 p.m.
we hung out and danced.

00:10:04.334 --> 00:10:05.400
-You were so fun.

00:10:05.400 --> 00:10:06.767
Though, I have
to thank you, though.

00:10:06.767 --> 00:10:08.667
You were so generous.
-You're acting is good.

00:10:08.667 --> 00:10:10.667
My acting is terrible.
You can act.

00:10:10.667 --> 00:10:12.300
You can do everything.
-But you can dance.

00:10:12.300 --> 00:10:14.367
See, I'm not a dancer.

00:10:14.367 --> 00:10:17.000
I was like,
"Sing the song and drag Dolly."

00:10:17.000 --> 00:10:18.701
I know that's how you felt.
-No way.

00:10:18.701 --> 00:10:20.434
We had the best time.
-But we did dance.

00:10:20.434 --> 00:10:22.801
And we did have fun.
-I want to show everyone a clip.

00:10:22.801 --> 00:10:24.000
-Can we show a little of it?
-Yeah.

00:10:24.000 --> 00:10:25.534
Here's Dolly and I...
-Okay.

00:10:25.534 --> 00:10:27.834
-...in "Dolly Parton's
Mountain Magic Christmas."

00:10:27.834 --> 00:10:29.234
Take a look!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:10:29.234 --> 00:10:32.868
♪ It's almost too early
for Christmas ♪

00:10:32.868 --> 00:10:36.200
-♪ Too soon
to be singing this song ♪

00:10:36.200 --> 00:10:40.167
-♪ There's still
Halloween decorations ♪

00:10:40.167 --> 00:10:43.634
-♪ And haters will say
that it's wrong ♪

00:10:43.634 --> 00:10:47.634
-♪ Let's turn on the lights
for Mariah ♪

00:10:47.634 --> 00:10:51.200
-♪ To Rudolph
to shine up his nose ♪

00:10:51.200 --> 00:10:55.067
-♪ It's almost too early
for Christmas ♪

00:10:55.067 --> 00:10:59.367
♪ But why don't
we see how it goes ♪

00:10:59.367 --> 00:11:01.467
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Aww!

00:11:01.467 --> 00:11:04.133
-Come on, now!
Come on!

00:11:04.133 --> 00:11:05.868
That's how you do it!
-Yeah, we do!

00:11:05.868 --> 00:11:07.501
-Dolly Parton!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:11:07.501 --> 00:11:09.567
"Dolly Parton's
Mountain Magic Christmas"

00:11:09.567 --> 00:11:13.434
airs tomorrow night at 8:00 p.m.
right here on NBC!

00:11:13.434 --> 00:11:15.434
We're talking more with Dolly
after the break.

00:11:15.434 --> 00:11:16.968
Come on back, everybody.

